May I introduce you my chess game. I'm pretty sure I forgot to implement some game rules: just movement and capture feature are implemented. I didn't have time to animate it (it was out of the scope of my project). To play:
1) click a piece you want to move. A special indicator appear around the piece;
2) all cell you can move to are put in evidence by a red spot;
3) all pieces you can capture are surrounded by a red ring;
4) click the cell you want to move your piece o the piece you want to capture;
5) use key "A" and "D" to rotate the game board to have a better view of the game;

Made with a tutorial by BMo:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YHSanceczXY&t=112s.
Change Log: 
1) Menu added;
2) Little ball bouncing changes;
3) At each paddle interact the ball is faster;
4) At each round ball speed returns to original value;

This project/challenge of Unity Learn outlines four potential bonus features for the Driving Simulation Prototype at varying levels of difficulty:

Easy: Obstacle Pyramids
Medium: Oncoming vehicles
Hard: Camera switcher
Expert: Local multiplayer

The objective of each stage/level is to touch the signs that are at the end of the road. At the Expert Level, whoever touches first will win.

Controls and Commands:

Esc (escape): To close/exit game;

Easy Level:
* Move: A (turn left) W (forward) S (backward) D (turn right) or Arrows (⬅️ ⬆️ ⬇️ ➡️);

Medium Level:
* Move: A (turn left) W (forward) S (backward) D (turn right) or Arrows (⬅️ ⬆️ ⬇️ ➡️);

Hard Level:
* Move: A (turn left) W (forward) S (backward) D (turn right) or Arrows (⬅️ ⬆️ ⬇️ ➡️);
* Switch camera view: Space;

Expert Level:
* Move Player 1: A (tap left) W (ahead) S (aft) D (tap right);
* Switch camera view Player 1: Space;
* Move Player 2: Arrow (⬅️ ⬆️ ⬇️ ➡️);
*Switch Camera View Player 2: 0 (zero);

